--------------------------------

### Trust policy for an App Runner access role

Source: https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apprunner/latest/dg/security_iam_service-with-iam.html

This policy allows the App Runner build service principal to assume the role for accessing Amazon ECR images.

```JSON
{
  "Version":"2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {
        "Service": "build.apprunner.amazonaws.com"
      },
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole"
    }
  ]
}
```

--------------------------------

### Trust policy for an App Runner instance role

Source: https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apprunner/latest/dg/security_iam_service-with-iam.html

This policy allows the App Runner task service principal to assume the role for granting permissions to compute instances.

```JSON
{
  "Version":"2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {
        "Service": "tasks.apprunner.amazonaws.com"
      },
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole"
    }
  ]
}
```

--------------------------------

### IAM Policy for Private ECR Access

Source: https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock-agentcore/latest/devguide/harness-security.html

Use this policy to grant the harness permission to pull custom container images from a private ECR repository.

```JSON
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Sid": "ECRImageAccess",
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "ecr:GetDownloadUrlForLayer",
        "ecr:BatchGetImage"
      ],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:ecr:<ecrRegion>:<ecrAccountId>:repository/<ecrRepoName>"
    },
    {
      "Sid": "ECRTokenAccess",
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": "ecr:GetAuthorizationToken",
      "Resource": "*"
    }
  ]
}
```

### App Runner IAM roles > Service roles > Instance role

Source: https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apprunner/latest/dg/security_iam_service-with-iam.html

The instance role is an optional role that provides permissions to AWS service actions required by your application code running on compute instances. Because App Runner cannot anticipate specific API calls your code might make, you must create a custom policy and assign it to the instance role, ensuring the trust policy declares tasks.apprunner.amazonaws.com as a trusted entity.

