### Trust policy for an App Runner instance role

Source: https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apprunner/latest/dg/security_iam_service-with-iam.html

This policy allows the App Runner task service principal to assume the role for granting permissions to compute instances.

```JSON
{
  "Version":"2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {
        "Service": "tasks.apprunner.amazonaws.com"
      },
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole"
    }
  ]
}
```

--------------------------------

### IAM Permission Policy for Secrets Manager Sources

Source: https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/pipeline-iam-reference.html

Allows the pipeline role to retrieve secrets from AWS Secrets Manager and decrypt them using a customer-managed KMS key.

```json
{
    "Version": "2012-10-17",
    "Statement": [
        {
            "Sid": "secrets-manager-access",
            "Effect": "Allow",
            "Action": [
                "secretsmanager:GetSecretValue"
            ],
            "Resource": "arn:aws:secretsmanager:your-region:your-account-id:secret:your-secret-name*"
        },
        {
            "Sid": "kms-access",
            "Effect": "Allow",
            "Action": "kms:Decrypt",
            "Resource": "arn:aws:kms:your-region:your-account-id:key/your-key-id"
        }
    ]
}
```

--------------------------------

### Allow Bedrock to Decrypt Secrets Manager Secrets with KMS

Source: https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/encryption-kb.md

Attach this policy to your Amazon Bedrock service role to allow decryption of KMS-encrypted secrets in AWS Secrets Manager. Replace placeholder values with your specific AWS Region, account ID, and KMS key ID.

```json
{
    "Version":"2012-10-17",
    "Statement": [
        {
            "Effect": "Allow",
            "Action": [
                "kms:Decrypt"
            ],
            "Resource": [
                "arn:aws:kms:{{us-east-1}}:{{123456789012}}:key/{{key-id}}"
            ]
        }
    ]
}
```

--------------------------------

### Reference Secrets in Blueprint Configuration

Source: https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/CloudWatch_Synthetics_Canaries_MultiCheck_Blueprint.html

Syntax for referencing specific keys from an AWS Secret Manager secret within the authentication configuration.

```json


"Authentication": {
    "type": "BASIC",
    "username": ${AWS_SECRET:login/basic-auth-credentials:username},
    "password": ${AWS_SECRET:login/basic-auth-credentials:password}
}

```

### AWS Secrets Manager integration

Source: https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/CloudWatch_Synthetics_Canaries_MultiCheck_Blueprint.html

Synthetics integrates with AWS Secrets Manager to securely handle sensitive values like passwords or API keys. You can reference secrets directly in your configuration using a specific syntax for either the entire secret value or individual keys. To enable this, the canary's IAM role must have permissions for secretsmanager:GetSecretValue and secretsmanager:DescribeSecret. If the secret uses a customer-managed KMS key, the role also requires kms:Decrypt permissions.

